From kkelly at statsci.com  Tue Jan  2 18:29:55 2001
From: kkelly at statsci.com (Kim Kelly)
Date: Tue, 02 Jan 2001 10:29:55 -0800
Subject: Statistical Analysis of Financial Data in S-PLUS course
Message-ID: <00c001c074ea$01b85200$4e6410ac@statsci.com>

Statistical Analysis of Financial Data in S-PLUS presented by Dr. Rene
Carmona
New York, NY - http://www.splus.com/train/carmona.html

Course Description: This lecture style course is designed to show how S-PLUS
can be used in the analysis of financial data. The applications include:
correlation and risk measures, high frequency data integration, implied
information and alternative valuation of derivative securities, term
structure of interest rates modeling, stochastic volatility, and physical
time series (temperature, precipitation, etc.) for weather risk analysis.
The statistical concepts and methodologies which will be covered include:
heavy tails and extreme value distributions, principal component analysis,
parametric and nonparametric regressions, fitting time series and state
space models, filtering and prediction, Monte Carlo simulations and scenario
generation. Illustrations will include methods available with the latest
version of S-PLUS and a set of tools developed by the speaker. This course
will provide participants with a strong foundation for conducting analyses
of financial data.

Dates/City:     Feb 28 - Mar 1, 2001 New York, NY

*This course is offered as a two-day course but the topics covered each day
are fairly independent of each other. Therefore, either day can be taken
separately as a one-day course.
