Most of the GUI function code have been sorted out, except for a problem 
that we have with the GUI callback function which we want to use in a 
dynamic manner to populate list boxs, dialog headers and help information.

Heres a simple example of what we want to do...

We want to present a list of objects to the student as a pick list using a 
list box - the list is created dynamically when the function runs and the 
results stored in a character vector.

