From A.Christmann at HRZ.Uni-Dortmund.DE  Fri Jan  5 09:02:51 2001
From: A.Christmann at HRZ.Uni-Dortmund.DE (Christmann, Andreas)
Date: Fri, 05 Jan 2001 10:02:51 +0100
Subject: Re: comparison of correlation coefficients
References: <IJBGAIIIJKMGEAAA@mailcity.com>
Message-ID: <3A558DBA.BE99352A@HRZ.Uni-Dortmund.DE>

Dear Mr. Horwath,

perhaps the following S-Plus code may be helpful to you.

The first one computes Spearman's rank correlation coefficient and
an  asymptotic (1-alpha) confidence interval.
The second one uses a general connection between tests and confidence intervals
to construct an asymptotic level alpha test for the equality of two
Spearman rank correlation coefficients.
This may be helpful to you if both datasets (x1,x2) and (y1,y2) are assumed to 
be independent.

Of course, there is no warranty for the S-Plus functions.

Yours sincerely,
Andreas

#
# Spearman's rank correlation coefficient and
# asymptotic (1-alpha) confidence interval
#
spearmanci <- function(x,y, alpha=0.05) {
 epsilon <- 1.E-9
 notna <- !is.na(x + y) #exclude NAs
 n <- length(x[notna])
 rho <- c(rho = cor(rank(x[notna]), rank(y[notna])))
 CIlower <- NA
 CIupper <- NA
 z <- NA
 if (rho < 1-epsilon) {
  n <- length(x[notna])
  z <- 0.5 * ( log( (1+rho) / (1-rho) ) )
  lower <- z - qnorm(1-(alpha/2)) / sqrt(n)
  upper <- z + qnorm(1-(alpha/2)) / sqrt(n)
  CIlower <- (exp(2*lower)-1)/(exp(2*lower)+1)
  CIupper <- (exp(2*upper)-1)/(exp(2*upper)+1)
 }
 return(list(rho=rho,CIlower=CIlower,CIupper=CIupper,n=n, z=z))
}
### Example:
# tmpr <-spearmanci(rnorm(10),rnorm(10))

#
# Asymptotic level alpha test for equality of
# two Spearman's rank correlation coefficients
# based on an (asymptotic) 1-alpha confidence
# interval.
# Decision for alternative hypothesis (i.e. unequality "H1")
# if the confidence interval does NOT include the value zero.
#
spearmanci2 <- function(x1,x2,y1,y2,alpha=0.05) {
 tmp1 <- spearmanci(x1,x2)
 tmp2 <- spearmanci(y1,y2)
 diffrho <- as.double(tmp1$rho - tmp2$rho)
 diffz <- as.double(tmp1$z - tmp2$z)
 lower <- diffz - qnorm(1-(alpha/2)) * sqrt( (1/tmp1$n) + (1/tmp2$n) )
 upper <- diffz + qnorm(1-(alpha/2)) * sqrt( (1/tmp1$n) + (1/tmp2$n) )
 decision <- "H0"
 if ( lower < 0 && upper < 0 ) decision <- "H1"
 if ( lower > 0 && upper > 0 ) decision <- "H1"
 return(list(rho1=as.double(tmp1$rho),rho2=as.double(tmp2$rho), diffrho=diffrho,
             diffz=diffz, CIlower=lower,CIupper=upper, decision=decision))
}
### Example:
x1 <- c(rnorm(398),NA,NA); x2 <- 0.1*x1+rnorm(400)
y1 <- rt(400,3); y2 <- 0.3*y1+rt(400,5)
spearmanci2(x1,x2,y1,y2)

