On Tue, 9 Jan 2001, Paul Lin wrote:

> Hi Fellow Splus Colleagues,
>
> Here is a programming if question I wonder if someone has a handle on.
>
> In the following pseudo-code:
>
>     if (condition) {
>         df <- df2
>     }
>
> when the if-condition is true, Splus will assign df2 to df.  The problem
> is that Splus will also print out the content of df2 or df.  This
> becomes really (really) slow when df2 is of Texas size.
>
> Does anyone know how to turn off this print-to-screen feature?

invisible().  The last expression in a condition is returned, and printed
at top level. So make it invisible(df <- df2) or add invisible()

