I came across this when I used survfit and coxph in a program.
I wanted survival estimates of more than a few observations in
the dummy data set (for example, the dummy data set may be the
data set fitted by coxph). However, for each observation, survfit
returns the estimates from all strata, not just those from the
stratum to which the observation belongs, which are what I
wanted. To get what I wanted, I have to figure out the strata
information for each observation. If survfit is used in a
command line with 1 or 2 observations, it is not difficult to
see by eyes which strata these observations belong to.
