"Hebborn, Ansgar {PBSE~Basel}" wrote:
> 
> I am working with a S-Plus 2000 dataframe (1 record per patient) and would 
> like 
> to assign the maximum of 7 variables in each row ("record") to a new variable 
> in this
> dataframe. 

Consider the following matrix

  > A <- matrix(c(5,4,3,1,6,5), 2)
  > A
       [,1] [,2] [,3] 
  [1,]    5    3    6
  [2,]    4    1    5

The command

  > apply(A, 1, max)
  [1] 6 5

produces a vector containing the max of each row, and to get
the max for each column, u can use

  > apply(A, 2, max)
  [1] 5 3 6

So, to add an column containing the max of the rows, u simply
need to type

  > A.new <- cbind(A, apply(A,1,max))
  > A.new
       [,1] [,2] [,3] [,4] 
  [1,]    5    3    6    6
  [2,]    4    1    5    5

The same applies to dataframes...

