From AnnisC at ASME.org  Wed Jan 17 04:02:42 2001
From: AnnisC at ASME.org (Charles Annis, P.E.)
Date: Tue, 16 Jan 2001 23:02:42 -0500
Subject: SUMMARY: corrupted defaults
Message-ID: <004d01c0803a$57d354e0$8c8324cf@ggvjd>

S-Plusers:

 

Earlier today I wrote that:using S-Plus 2000 I seem to have 
corrupted some default settings so that now for plots generated using the linear 
regression option of the GUI, the background color is dark red, rather than 
transparent.  

 

The suggestion that worked is to delete the _prefs file, and 
let S-Plus rebuild an uncorruped one.  

 

My situation was a bit more complicated than most because I 
also have installed Professor Meeker's SLIDA (Splus Functions for Life Data 
Analysis, http://www.public.iastate.edu/~stat533/slida.html) 
and some coordination among the _prefs folders is called for.

 

It was also suggested that the only file that needed to be 
rebuilt was axclass.dft, but after deleting the _prefs file, and re-starting 
S-Plus 200 and having the problem NOT fixed, I looked a bit further.  A few 
months ago there was a conflict between the SLIDA _prefs and the standard issue 
_prefs, that Professor Meeker resolved.  Thus I had to delete the 
_prefs folder in my SLIDA directory; the one in the sp2000 directory being 
superfluous for SLIDA users.  Upon re-starting S-Plus, SLIDA rebuilt the 
missing _prefs, and a new SLIDA GUI, and the problem of dark-red background was 
vanquished.

 

My thanks to all who helped, especially to Chuck Taylor, David 
Smith, and Naomi Robbins.

