S-users:

Thank you for all the reply to my query. The answer to my query was of
course:
> paste(c(5, 6.5, 9), collapse="-")  

The mistake I made when trying to figure out this command is worth
knowing for all the lazy people like me. I took the bad habit to
abbreviate the arguments in an S call. The first command I tried in this
case was paste(c(5, 6.5, 9), col="-"), which does not give he desired
result. I did not think that the mistake was due to the abbreviation.
The lesson I learned is that we can abbreviate the arguments (up to
uniqueness) UNLESS they follow the argument "..." in the function call,
which is the case in paste:

> args(paste)
function(..., sep = " ", collapse = NULL)

Olivier

