Subject: The correlation principle
Message-ID: <3A6DE29C.3604D6FA@selway.umt.edu>

A little known principle:
The Correlation Principle for estimation of parameter theta:
A statistical inference or procedure should be consistent with the
assumption that any explanation of a set of data should be accompanied
by theta-hat, a value of theta, that makes some correlation coefficient
zero.
