              Andreas Krause

>Thanks to Bob Byers for supplying a report (offending files) 
program >(see below), which indeed pointed to those above listed 
strangers:

Here is a function that will list all the offending files
at once. (provided to me by MathSoft a long time ago, but 
still works.)
Good luck,
Bob Byers

report.foreign.objects<-
function(where = 1:length(search()))
{
for(db in where)
for(nm in objects(db))
if(!exists(nm, where = db)) warning(paste(sep = "", 
  "foreign object with name \"", nm, 
  "\" on database ", db))
        
invisible()
}

>And Scott Chasalow also issued a warning like Andreas:

Hoi,

It sounds like you have put files in _data from outside S+.  This is
something you should NEVER do.  Only S+ should write files to 
_data, and
only automatically (it saves S+ objects there).  By this last, I mean 
that
if you explicitly save a script, or a graph, or export to a file an S+
object using dump() or sink() or such, these files also must not be 
put in
_data.

Ik hoop dat dat duidelijk is...

Groeten,
Scott

