Dear S-plusers,

Can anyone please tell me where I might find codes for clustering and
discrimination that measure "distance" between entities using a
mahalanobis metric?

I have a large number of temperature profiles (temperature vs. depth),
which I want to group according to shape.  Variability can depend on
depth, and values at nearby depths can be correlated.  I think that
"squared distance" between profiles might best be expressed as
      (t1-t2)'V^{-1}(t1-t2), 
where t1 and t2 are vectors of temperatures at specified depths,
V^{-1} is the inverse of the covariance matrix, and matrix
multiplication is implied.  Each cluster would have a mean vector and
a covariance matrix.

