Hi Susan,

I think that trying to do the whole thing using a graphsheet is definitely
not a good idea.

What others I know have done in the past is to create a poster in Powerpoint
(!!!) and import the graphs as .wmf files using the Insert | Picture | From
File... menus. Use the File | Page Setup menus to create a custom page size
of 36" by 36" to get the right size poster.

The extent to which this works will depend also on what the printer you're
printing to expects. If it's a postscript printer, you probably want to
distill the powerpoint file thru Adobe Acrobat Distiller first.

Of course, this all assumes you want to stay within the Microsoft world.

Hope this helps.

