1)  These models are not nested LS fits, so you can conclude very
little from what you showed us.  Increasing the df does not necesarily
improve the fit.

2) df = 1 makes no sense.  The model includes a linear term and
a non-linear term zero, and you have given the latter 0 df.
Indeed, s() says:

   Values for df should be greater than 1.

summary() will tell you a lot more, including

DF for Terms and Chi-squares for Nonparametric Effects

             Df Npar Df Npar Chisq    P(Chi) 
 (Intercept)  1                             
           x  1                             
s(y, df = 4)  1       4   2.239815 0.6876443

Yes, it looks as if df has to be at least 5. 

I suggest you try regression splines instead.

