16 1  1.83562547     4    1
17 2  0.63651418     5    1
18 3 -1.37934738     5   NA
19 4 -0.24545963     5   NA
20 5  0.35754048     5    1

Say I want to fit y on x for each group and I simply type
na.action=na.omit because I suspect there may be missing data (even
though there is not):

> lmList(y~x|group,data=junk,na.action=na.omit)
Problem in lm.fit.qr(unset(x), unset(y)): computed fit is singular, rank 1 
Use traceback() to see the call stack
Call:
  Model: y ~ x | group 
   Data: junk 

Coefficients:
  (Intercept)           x 
1  -5.0913160  1.23805388
2          NA          NA
3  -1.2329636  0.78466873
4   2.2803619 -0.56482898
5   0.8224967 -0.09299124

Degrees of freedom: 9 total; 1 residual
Residual standard error: 0.6123541

Notice it eliminates perfectly good rows and gives poor estimates.

If I exclude the columns with missing data:

> lmList(y~x|group,data=junk[,1:3], na.action=na.omit)
Call:
  Model: y ~ x | group 
   Data: junk[, 1:3] 

Coefficients:
  (Intercept)           x 
1  -3.0453192  0.74318013
