Here is a neat way to use the outer function, to simplify the 
Splus function ar.acf, that I sent as a response to using ar.acf

Hello,

Tom here at Insightful, just an idea, it illustrates some options in
S and removes the for loop in ar.acf.  It also illustrates the mechanics behind
the ar.acf estimator. ar.acf1 is faster than ar.acf when  p>6

This is a different  way to calculate ar.acf

ar.acf1 <-
function(phi, nlags = length(phi))
{
        p <- length(phi)
        seqp <- seq(p)
        L1 <- c(phi, rep(0, p))
        L2 <- c(rep(0, p), phi)
        M1 <- L1[outer(seqp, seqp, "+")]
        M2 <- L2[p + outer(seqp, seqp, "-")]
        rho <- solve(diag(p) - structure(M1 + M2, dim = c(p, p)), phi)
        nleft <- nlags - p
        if(nleft > 0) {
                rho <- c(rho, rep(0, nleft))
                for(k in 1:nleft)
                        rho[k + p] <- sum(phi * rho[(k + p - 1):k])
        }
        else rho <- rho[1:nlags]
        rho
}
> 

