Here is a simple abs function, that is nicely continuous with derivatives of all
orders.

abs.1
function(x, delta)
{
        y <- sqrt(x^2 + delta^2)
        y <- y - delta^2/y
        return(y)
}

It is asymptotically abs(x) for large x and x^2/(2*delta) for small x.
Note that the abs.1(x) <= abs(x) for all x.

Just a thought, Its probably been used somewhere else... 

