Don,

You can add the function yourself, 
I created a paramter delta that is in position 1, because of the D function
using its own call routine ... anyway:

Create abs.1 the alternate, note delta is defined out of scope (position 1 or 0)

 abs.1 
function(x)
{
        y <- sqrt(x^2 + delta^2)
        y <- y - delta^2/y
        return(y)
}

Use the deriv function to get the derivative !

> abs.1deriv<-deriv(~ sqrt(x^2+delta^2) -
delta^2/sqrt(x^2+delta^2),c("x"),function(x) NULL)

You may want to modify the function to remove the attributes and directly
calculate the derivative and return .grad
as in:

abs.1deriv<-
function(x)
{
        .expr2 <- delta^2
        .expr3 <- (x^2) + .expr2
        .expr4 <- sqrt(.expr3)
        .expr10 <- 0.5 * ((2 * x) * (.expr3^-0.5))
        .value <- .expr4 - (.expr2/.expr4)
        .actualArgs <- match.call()["x"]
        .grad <- .expr10 + ((.expr2 * .expr10)/(.expr4^2))
}

Now, add the following line in the D function:

abs.1 = make.call("*", make.call("abs.1deriv", expr[[2]]),D(expr[[2]], name)),

just before the following line:
                
exp = make.call("*", expr, D(expr[[2]], name)),

